cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its benchmarks, please cite both the software and the accompanying article."
title: "From Intent to Slice: Explainable and Agentic AI for Trustworthy Network Slice Selection"
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation, frozen benchmarks, experiment runners and
  We evaluate an explainable slice selector on 3,000 synthetic network intents, 
  finding 91.7% mean accuracy across five seeds and an increase from 90.3% to 91.9% with a 
  TF-IDF prior on the seed-46 test split. In a separate 100-intent trial, the tool-using 
  LLM agent achieved 100% contract validity but 87.0% accuracy and 35.65 seconds per intent, 
  highlighting trade-offs among validation, accuracy, and latency.
  
